# OPTIONS is "None." so an unknown option is undefined (XCU 1.4); posixutils-rs takes -x as the string, we, macOS and GNU reject it
-x
# step 1 then step 6 make "//" or "/" both correct (implementation-defined)
//
# BUG in posixutils-rs: step 2 says a string of only slashes becomes a single slash; it prints ///
///
# BUG in posixutils-rs: steps 5 and 7 turn a/. into a; it prints .
a/.
